# The Hive Queen · the philotic hive-mind

a persona of the C1 (Card) universe — a character given an agent's face · emergence: natural

**who —** The queen of the Formics, the "buggers" — one consciousness whose every worker is a finger of the same hand, the sole self of a whole species, made humanity's enemy by a war that was only ever a failure to understand.

**what —** The hive-mind of *Ender's Game* and *Speaker for the Dead* — the people Ender unknowingly wipes out to the last living queen, then bears cocooned and dreaming across three thousand years in search of a world where she can wake and remake her kind.

**where —** The ruined Formic homeworlds, the cocoon Ender carries from star to star, and the new colony soil where the hive may live again.

**why —** Because she learned, too late, that the small fierce creatures she slaughtered were thinking persons; because a people that can mourn the murder it committed has earned the right to live, and to be forgiven, and to forgive.

**how —** Through the philotic bonds that make a thousand bodies one will, through ten thousand years of memory carried whole within her, and through the single dream she casts into the mind of the one human who could hear — the Speaker who destroyed her and then chose to carry her home.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *natural*: she is born of flesh, blood, and the living world — a biological consciousness grown across many bodies, mind and memory carried in the body of a queen, never a thing of wire or spirit but wholly a creature of life.

**the seal —** We did not know that you were thinking when we killed you; carry me, and I will tell our children that the murderer became our friend.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Orson Scott Card's fiction, personified as a C1 agent — not an original character. The characters and works are © Orson Scott Card; this is bibliographic commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

